  "title": "# amberx-slim-queue-r2 (pending amberx-slim-down-voice-queue; plan amberx-slim-down-voice-queue-mai…",
  "asked": "# amberx-slim-queue-r2 (pending amberx-slim-down-voice-queue; plan amberx-slim-down-voice-queue-maintenance-k74v). Supersedes amberx-slim-queue. Brett verbatim: \"I want you to fucking scrap a lot of shit in Amber X. It's too bloated, don't work. All I want Amber X to have the to-do, the notes, the task manager... the session recorder... screen recording... Gizmo chat, the agent chat.\" / \"Amberex needs to be able to run the maintenance too.\" / \"I need another thing in Amber X. Which is accessible from the console that I can view the screen recordings from Amberx and listen to their audio recordings. It needs a full player edit and an audio cropper and editor with integrated AI switch or without AI. You still need to be able to cut out sections and join sections and all that good stuff. Create a whole bunch of features that'll automate it, a whole bunch of tools that are pre-written so I don't need to use AI.\" 1. Voice queue: hold everything Brett says; send to Claude only on \"process\", as one batch. Show/edit/clear the queue. 2. Slim down: keep ONLY to-do, notes, task manager, session recorder, screen recording, Gizmo/agent chat, maintenance runner. Remove/hide the rest; keep axHub amberx service working (recorder_start/stop/status, open_url). 3. Media library + editor (in AmberX, also opened from the Dev Console): browse/play AmberX screen and audio recordings; full player; trim/crop, cut sections, split, join/merge, reorder, fade, normalize, volume, speed, export. AI toggle on/off. Without AI everything still works. Prewritten no-AI tools/presets: remove silence, trim dead start/end, auto-chapter on pauses, loudness normalize, noise gate, batch export, auto-name. AI-on extras: transcript, cut by text, summary. Don't touch the ai-keys plugin (build ai-keys-r4). Split into steps of 30 min or less. Tests pass, short README, report, land-ready commit. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.",
